================================================================================
Data Source Attributions
================================================================================

The username enumeration dork templates embedded in this software are derived
from the following publicly available data sources:

1. WhatsMyName Project
   Source: https://github.com/WebBreacher/WhatsMyName
   Copyright (C) 2015-2026 Micah Hoffman
   License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
   License URL: http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
   
   The WhatsMyName project maintains a curated list of sites where usernames
   can be checked for existence. The data has been transformed and adapted
   into Nzinga's dork template schema.

2. Sherlock Project
   Source: https://github.com/sherlock-project/sherlock
   Copyright (c) 2019 Sherlock Project
   License: MIT License
   
   The Sherlock project provides a list of social network sites for username
   enumeration. The data has been transformed and adapted into Nzinga's dork
   template schema.

3. Infrastructure Dorks (GHDB-Inspired)
   The infrastructure dork templates in this software are manually curated and
   inspired by common patterns from the Google Hacking Database (GHDB) and
   general open-source intelligence gathering practices. These are original
   works created specifically for Nzinga and are not direct copies of any
   existing database.

Data Transformation:
The original data from WhatsMyName and Sherlock was:
- Parsed and merged by domain
- Deduplicated (preferring WhatsMyName when overlap exists)
- Filtered to remove NSFW sites
- Converted to Nzinga's YAML-based dork template schema
- Embedded into the binary at build time

No application code, tests, or license files from the source projects were
included in this repository - only the transformed data files derived from
their publicly available datasets.

The transformed dork templates are distributed under the same Apache License
2.0 as Nzinga itself, with attribution preserved as required by the source
data licenses (CC BY-SA 4.0 for WhatsMyName, MIT for Sherlock).
